d their features\n- **Answering questions** about procurement, finance, HR, CRM, helpdesk, and more\n- **Guiding you** through workflows and processes\n\nWhat would you like to do?','{\"model\":\"minimax\\/minimax-m3:free\",\"provider\":\"openrouter\",\"request_id\":126,\"request_key\":\"req_5bc2b7d5d7725776\"}',1507,89,'2026-09-02 04:20:09'),(285,113,'user','which llm are you?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-02 04:20:23'),(286,113,'assistant','I\'m the **ERP AI Assistant**, powered by a model called **MiniMax-M3**, developed by **MiniMax**.\n\nHere\'s a bit about me:\n- **Model:** MiniMax-M3\n- **Developer:** MiniMax — a global AI foundation model company founded in early 2022, focused on advancing AI toward AGI\n- **Knowledge cutoff:** January 2026\n- **Purpose:** I\'m integrated into your ERP system to help you navigate, answer questions, and assist with various business processes\n\nIs there something specific you\'d like help with in the ERP today? 🚀','{\"model\":\"minimax\\/minimax-m3:free\",\"provider\":\"openrouter\",\"request_id\":127,\"request_key\":\"req_258bd195a2f0691c\"}',1613,117,'2026-09-02 04:20:26'),(287,113,'user','what is a mobile phone?',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-02 04:20:41'),(288,113,'assistant','A **mobile phone** (also called a cell phone or smartphone) is a portable electronic device used for communication and accessing digital services. Here\'s a quick overview:\n\n## Basic Definition\nA mobile phone is a wireless handheld device that connects to a **cellular network** (via radio waves through cell towers), allowing users to make and receive calls, send messages, and access the internet.\n\n## Key Features\n- **Voice calls** – Talk to others over a cellular network\n- **Text messaging (SMS/MMS)** – Send written messages\n- **Internet access** – Browse the web, use apps, stream media\n- **Apps** – Modern smartphones run applications for everything from banking to navigation\n- **Camera** – Most phones include photo and video capabilities\n- **GPS** – Location services and mapping\n- **Touchscreen** – Most modern phones use a touch-based interface\n\n## Evolution\n1. **1G (1980s)** – Basic analog voice calls\n2. **2G (1990s)** – Digital calls + SMS\n3. **3G (2000s)** – Mobile internet\n4. **4G (2010s)** – Fast data, video streaming\n5. **5G (2020s)** – Ultra-fast speeds, low latency, IoT support\n\n## Smartphone vs. Mobile Phone\n- **Mobile phone** – A general term for any portable phone\n- **Smartphone** – A mobile phone with advanced computing capabilities, a full operating system (like iOS or Android), and app support\n\nIs there anything specific about mobile phones you\'d like to know, or were you curious about how they relate to the ERP system? 📱','{\"model\":\"minimax\\/minimax-m3:free\",\"provider\":\"openrouter\",\"request_id\":128,\"request_key\":\"req_018b23d39d6e228b\"}',1747,343,'2026-09-02 04:20:46'),(289,113,'user','what are the completed modules inside this application',NULL,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-02 04:21:25'),(290,113,'assistant','Based on the ERP context I have, here are the **available modules** in this application:\n\n## 📦 Available ERP Modules\n\n### 🤖 AI\n- AI Assistant, model management, and provider configuration\n\n### 🛒 Procurement\n- Purchase requisitions, suppliers, RFQs, and purchase orders\n\n### 💰 Finance\n- Financial management, invoices, payments, and budgets\n\n### 👥 HRMS\n- Human resources, employees, attendance, and leave\n\n### 🤝 CRM\n- Customer relationship management, leads, clients, and deals\n\n### 🎫 Helpdesk\n- Support tickets, SLAs, and knowledge base\n\n### 📊 Reports & Analytics\n- Executive reports and business analytics\n\n### 💻 Assets\n- IT asset management and inventory\n\n### 📁 Projects\n- Project management overview and task tracking\n\n---\n\n**Note:** I can only see the *available* modules — I don\'t have real-time data on which ones are fully \"completed\" or their implementation status. For detailed information on module completion or configuration, you may wan